    {"number":1,"wpId":50409,"title":"Practical Usage – Level 1.1 – Long Call","duration":"Reading","type":"text","vimeoId":null,"section":"Module 1: Long Call Foundations","contentHtml":"<p>In this lesson, we practice buying a call option on the ThinkOrSwim trading platform. A long call is a bullish options strategy that gives you the right to buy a stock at a specific strike price before expiration.</p><h3>Step-by-Step Guide</h3><ol><li>Log in to the ThinkOrSwim platform.</li><li>Open the Trade tab and select the Options section.</li><li>Search for the stock you want to trade.</li><li>Choose the call option with the preferred strike price and expiration.</li><li>Enter the number of contracts and review the order.</li><li>Confirm and send the order.</li></ol><p>Observe how stock-price movement, volatility and time decay affect the position's potential profit or loss.</p>"},
